# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
think	one
# "Think" means the same mental activity (thinking, as in doubting) in P3, P4 and P5. P5 only denies it ("if I had only ceased to think"). That is the same claim negated, not a new sense.
# There is a possible shift from what I can suppose (an epistemic matter) to what is really distinct (a metaphysical matter) between P1/P2 and C1/C. That would involve the word "suppose" against "distinct", but no claim shared across statements carries it. No premise or assumption is a bridge for it, so I name none.
